\",\"replacement\":\"The gateway refuses a request for three separate reasons, and only one of them is a cap\",\"reason\":\"Same statement as a40.\"},{\"segment\":\"b39\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"two of the three have nothing to do with how much traffic a caller has sent in the window it is currently in.\",\"reason\":\"Joined onto the three-reasons sentence.\"},{\"segment\":\"a41\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"A credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance, or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit, in which case it is refused before it has been read at all.\",\"reason\":\"Adds source_b's before-read detail.\"},{\"segment\":\"b40\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"A credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance, or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit, in which case it is refused before it has been read at all.\",\"reason\":\"Three causes and before-read detail carried.\"},{\"segment\":\"a43\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"The distinction matters more to a retry loop than it does to a reader.\",\"reason\":\"Takes source_b's comparison.\"},{\"segment\":\"b41\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"The distinction matters more to a retry loop than it does to a reader.\",\"reason\":\"Same point as a43.\"},{\"segment\":\"a44\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service, and the log afterwards shows nothing but a long run of refusals and no successes, which reads like an outage and isn’t one — and the wasted budget is the caller’s own.\",\"reason\":\"Joined with b43's outage point.\"},{\"segment\":\"b42\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"replacement\":\"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service\",\"reason\":\"a44 states the same point.\"},{\"segment\":\"b43\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"and the log afterwards shows nothing but a long run of refusals and no successes, which reads like an outage and isn’t one — and the wasted budget is the caller’s own.\",\"reason\":\"Log and budget points carried.\"},{\"segment\":\"a47\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"A cap can be raised, but not on the strength of an assertion that the current one is too small: the number of caps raised without a measurement behind them is 0.\",\"reason\":\"Joined with b46.\"},{\"segment\":\"b46\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"A cap can be raised, but not on the strength of an assertion that the current one is too small\",\"reason\":\"Joined with a47.\"},{\"segment\":\"a48\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Bring a full week of refusal counts, the shape of the traffic across the day, and the deadline that traffic is serving.\",\"reason\":\"Adds full from b47.\"},{\"segment\":\"b47\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"Bring a full week of refusal counts, the shape of the traffic across the day, and the deadline that traffic is serving.\",\"reason\":\"Same list as a48.\"},{\"segment\":\"a49\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"Before it looks at the number at all, the platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty — a burst is cheaper to smooth than it is to serve at its peak.\",\"reason\":\"Adds source_b's ordering detail.\"},{\"segment\":\"b48\",\"disposition\":\"subsumed\",\"replacement\":\"Before it looks at the number at all, the platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty\",\"reason\":\"Ordering detail carried.\"},{\"segment\":\"b49\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"replacement\":\"a burst is cheaper to smooth than it is to serve at its peak.\",\"reason\":\"a49 states the same point.\"},{\"segment\":\"a50\",\"disposition\":\"reworded\",\"replacement\":\"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually gets what i